  "note": "calculateGold evaluates gold-rules.js and takes the MAX stage among fired rules (GOLD I default when none fire); the ABCD group is computed separately by determineAbcdGroup(). Several rule pairs are independent, not else-if branches, so both fire and both count toward the max when both thresholds are crossed (e.g. CAT >=10 and CAT >=20 both fire for a CAT score of 28). detectAdditionalFlags is fully independent of the stage/group. demographics.bmi is NOT auto-derived inside the grader from weight/height - the caller (form-app.js) computes it via calculateBMI() and stores it separately, so a persona state must set demographics.bmi explicitly or the BMI-gated rule/flag silently never fires even with weight and height both present.",
